          <p>Authenticators must be compliant with the most recent NIST Digital Identity Guidelines IAL, AAL, FAL level 3.</p>
          <p>IA-5 Guidance: FedRAMP requires that authentication assertions be encrypted when passed through third parties, such as a browser. For example, a SAML assertion can be encrypted using XML-Encryption, or an OpenID Connect ID Token can be encrypted using JSON Web Encryption (JWE).</p>
